  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Given name, often two (Juan Cruz, María Belén), then the father's surname; Argentines can legally add the mother's surname but most use one. Close to half of Argentines have Italian ancestors, so Italian surnames (Rossi, Ferrari, Romano) sit beside Spanish and Basque ones (González, Fernández, Echeverría). Recent favourites for babies include Mateo, Thiago, Benjamín, Bautista, Martina, Catalina and Delfina. Buenos Aires also has large Bolivian and Paraguayan communities with their own surnames (Mamani, Quispe, Benítez, Villalba), and families of Jewish, German, Polish and Armenian origin.",
